<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — MorphoEval overall 90.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py` (90.5/100, up from 57.3/100 in Pass 1; +33.2 points). The remediated script implements all 5 thermodynamic regimes of Steinberg (1963) and Graner & Glazier (1992) (`complete_engulfment`, `checkerboard_mixing`, `partial_engulfment`, `cell_dissociation`, and `equal_adhesion_control`), runs a 7-point continuous J_AB sweep across both phase boundaries (gamma_AB = 0 and gamma_AB = gamma_BM - gamma_AM = 6), segments the SHA-256-locked confocal embryoid body specimen (`cell_sorting_specimen.jpg`, radial profile correlation r = 0.9252, Δr = +0.2793 vs simulated Δr = +0.3672), validates Foty & Steinberg's (1996) 5-tissue Gallus gallus surface tension hierarchy (10/10 transitive pairs, r = 0.9959), and is backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_041_differential_adhesion_sorting.lean`. Overall 90.7/100 (faithfulness 89.8, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b9976f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/differential_adhesion_sorting_comparison.png: rendered output of 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py at b9976f8, image/png, 503094 B, 3000×1260 px, artifact_sha256 755cf4ee94bc2b8c291aaf3de87bc50d9a6d08ca0c35af27bb8e340856cc1c90 (sha256 755cf4ee94bc2b8c291aaf3de87bc50d9a6d08ca0c35af27bb8e340856cc1c90), spec_fingerprint 439c3a9015bc8fdc9014e2aa3a89cd71cffc876fcd81d0cb0b2f88bbf798d5a9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 439c3a9015bc8fdc9014e2aa3a89cd71cffc876fcd81d0cb0b2f88bbf798d5a9; artifact_sha256: 755cf4ee94bc2b8c291aaf3de87bc50d9a6d08ca0c35af27bb8e340856cc1c90. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-differential-adhesion-sorting-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Steinberg (1963, 1970) Differential Adhesion Hypothesis (DAH): dissociated binary embryonic tissues spontaneously sort into concentric core-shell or lens configurations governed by interfacial free energy minimization. | Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3: extended Cellular Potts Hamiltonian with interfacial tensions gamma_AB = J_AB - (J_AA + J_BB)/2 and gamma_tauM = J_tauM - J_tautau/2 partitioning parameter space into checkerboard (gamma_AB < 0), complete engulfment (0 < gamma_AB < gamma_BM - gamma_AM), partial engulfment (gamma_AB > gamma_BM - gamma_AM > 0), and dissociation (gamma_AM < 0). | Foty, Pfleger, Forgacs & Steinberg (1996) Development Table 1: empirical Gallus gallus tissue surface tensions (20.1 > 12.6 > 8.5 > 4.6 > 1.6 dyn/cm) strictly predict transitive mutual envelopment.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended Cellular Potts Model coupled with Detailed-Balance Kawasaki cell exchanges across all 5 thermodynamic regimes plus a 7-point continuous J_AB sweep. | Computer-vision segmentation of confocal fluorescence embryoid body spheroid (`cell_sorting_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against Potts core-shell profiles (r = 0.9252, RMSE = 0.210).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice Cellular Potts representation of 3D multicellular spheroid cross-sections.; does_not_claim: Does not model active chemotaxis or subcellular cadherin trafficking kinetics.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend the 2D Cellular Potts lattice to a 3D spherical lattice (N = 64^3) to compare 2D cross-sectional vs. full 3D power-law/logarithmic sorting exponents." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.07e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

